# CatDex — TypeScript

## Basics

- Strict typing; avoid `any`. Prefer `unknown` + narrow
- Domain types live in `src/types/` (`cat.ts`, …)
- Shared unions for gender, rarity UI ids, error kinds — don’t stringly-type across layers

## Imports

- Use `@/` alias for app code
- Prefer type-only imports when appropriate: `import type { Cat } from '@/types/cat'`

## Nullability

- Optional AI fields stay optional (`suggestedName?`, `tags?`)
- UI must handle missing analysis pieces with safe fallbacks (`formatCatDefaultName`, etc.)

## Server

- `server/src` uses Zod / schema modules for Vision payloads — keep client `CatAnalysis` and server normalize\* in sync when fields change

## Scripts

- App: `npm run typecheck`
- Don’t weaken `tsconfig` to silence errors — fix call sites
